  "body": "Follow-up from the review of PR #1216 (tool kind glyphs on the Tool library rows and the tool picker; `Refs #661`).\n\n`egui_app::tests::tool_icon_wiring` (`every_catalog_row_wears_its_kind_glyph`, `every_picker_item_wears_its_kind_glyph`) checks the pure functions that choose an icon. Neither test paints: both would still pass if the `glyph(...)` call were deleted from the row or the dropdown item. The reviewer confirmed the wiring by a throwaway kittest (all 29 catalog rows and all 13 kinds in the opened picker painted their kind's texture; accessible names unchanged), so nothing is wrong today - the pin is what is missing.\n\nAlso from that review: the doc comment on `tool_of_kind` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_icon_wiring.rs`) says it builds \"a real, valid tool\", but for 9 of the 13 kinds adding that tool to a document is refused - correct the comment.\n\nDone means: one kittest (about 60 lines, under a second) loads the icon set, opens the Tool library page and the picker's dropdown, and asserts each tool kind's texture id is among the painted shapes of its row / item, driven from the kind list (items below the dropdown's scroll fold covered by a second pass or a taller popup); row and item accessible names asserted unchanged; the comment corrected. Do this after PR #1216 has merged (it merges at the next cut).\n",
